trends and their relative strengths for each commodity. An important difference
between this system and many other trend-following programs is the mathematical
determination of the size of the component portfolio positions based on the
volatility characteristics of the individual commodities and the overall
strength of the price trend. The basic risk management approach attempts to
prohibit any one position
 
