<PAGE>   122
 
to a liability for which recourse of creditors is limited is included in the
assets of a limited partnership only to the extent that the fair value of the
property exceeds that liability. Under the New York Act, a limited partner who
received such a prohibited distribution and who knew that the distribution
violated the New York Act is liable to the limited partnership for the amount of
the distribution for a period of three years from the date of the distribution.
This section of the New York Act does not affect any obligation or liability of
a limited partner under the Limited Partnership Agreement or other applicable
law (including relevant fraudulent conveyance acts) for the amount of a
distribution.
 
