WILLOWBRIDGE'S SYSTEMS, APPROACHES AND PROGRAMS (PAGE 86)
 
     For each of the Systems, risk is managed on a market level as well as on an
overall portfolio level. On the market level, risk is managed primarily by
utilizing proprietary volatility filters. When these filters detect a certain
excessive level of volatility in the markets traded, they will signal that the
Systems should no longer be trading in the markets in which the filters have
detected excessive volatility. In this way, the Systems do not participate in
markets in which there are extremes in market action. On the portfolio level,
risk is managed by utilizing a proprietary portfolio cutback rule. When
cumulative profits have reached a certain level, this rule determines that the
positions should be halved across the portfolio. In this way, risk is reduced
while allowing the Systems to continue to participate in the markets, albeit at
a reduced level. After the portfolio has been traded at half, the rule will then
determine when to increase positions to trade again at the full level.
 
     In connection with Willowbridge, the term "trading system" refers to a
computerized technical, systematic trading program of Willowbridge, the term
"trading approach" refers to a discretionary trading program of Willowbridge,
and the term "trading strategy" refers to either a trading system or a trading
approach. Willowbridge's trading strategies are available only through one of
its four "investment programs". An investment program consists of one or more
trading strategies or a combination thereof. For purposes of the past
performance presentation herein, each of the terms "trading system", "trading
approach", "trading strategy" and "investment program" means a "trading program"
as defined in Part 4 of the regulations of the CFTC.
 
